# LaTeX build artifacts
*.aux
*.log
*.out
*.fls
*.fdb_latexmk
*.synctex.gz
*.bbl
*.blg

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Matplotlib / font / OS caches
.cache/
.mplconfig/
.DS_Store

# Large binaries
*.pdf
*.mp4

# Vendored third-party assets (mujoco_menagerie model zoo, >1 GB of meshes)
external_deps/

# Vendored mesh assets and regenerable simulation logs
*.stl
*.STL
*.npz

# Generated terrain/torque MJCF variants written into results/ by the
# benchmarks. Regenerable, and they embed an absolute machine-local
# meshdir, so they must not be committed.
**/results/g1_wbc_torque_*.xml

# EXCEPTION: v5's G1 meshes ARE tracked. They are the 12-DoF legs-only G1 from
# unitree_rl_gym, and three of the 27 (torso_link_23dof_rev_1_0.STL and the two
# *_wrist_roll_rubber_hand.STL) have no mujoco_menagerie equivalent -- those
# three are also the largest, 14.8 of the 25.2 MB -- so no auto-fetch fallback
# can reconstruct this set. Committing them is the only way v5 reproduces from
# a clean checkout. v3/v4 meshes stay ignored: robot_descriptions supplies them.
!versions/v5/code/g1_description/meshes/*.STL
